# Rust build artifacts
/target/
**/*.rs.bk

# Cargo.lock is deliberately NOT ignored.
#
# This is a binary crate, not a library, so the lockfile is part of the build
# definition, not a local convenience: it pins every transitive version of
# `hound`, `serde` and friends. Ignore it and each build silently resolves
# whatever crates.io serves that day -- a dependency can change behaviour, or
# fail to compile, with no commit to point at.
#
# It was previously ignored here, which is why the repo had no lockfile at all
# and why CI had to run `cargo generate-lockfile` before every build.
